/*
 * Shared test fixture — not shipped in any package.
 *
 * A real EDSY SLEF export of a hull-tanked Anaconda (22 `Modules` entries).
 *
 * Contributed 2026-08-28 UTC by the repository owner from their own commander's fleet. Source text
 * SHA-256 `0486b2b31c0504f5074a75f6dcfeb935fc38d855c2fb8fcde57b818f9264bdb5`. Stored-form SHA-256
 * `aead9f6847b8eec1c419a4e9ce66dcf4129aea3a3e9ad170ac205332b2fc5199`. Its `ShipName`, `ShipIdent`
 * and the `appURL` holding the same build are kept: they describe a ship, not a person.
 *
 * Its `FrameShiftDrive` is the tech-broker pre-engineered SCO drive with Mass Manager added after
 * purchase, and it is the ground truth for a capture whose producer stores the modifier rather than
 * the modified value: EDSY re-derives every figure from the stock stat, writing the article's 2 s
 * boot time as `2.000122` and its 3536 t optimal mass as `3536.025391`. Frontier's own float32
 * precision does not reach that far, so identification is what the file pins — the drive is
 * unrecognized at journal tolerance, and an editor then refuses every engineering edit on it. The
 * port reproduces EDSY's own exported `MaxJumpRange` of 42.468335 ly for the fit.
 *
 * The capture is Elite Dangerous game output and remains the property of Frontier Developments
 * plc, redistributed under Frontier's media-usage terms; see ATTRIBUTIONS.md.
 *
 * A stored checksum here is of the payload alone, taken with this header comment removed; a source
 * checksum is of the upstream file as it was received.
 */
